From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean O'Hollaren <sean.ohollaren@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:14:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] FM-1: drive on KNOB 3 and the music's instrument on PRESETS;
 EDIT puts all the sound back

fm1_drive.h is a soft clipper over everything the game plays, ahead of the filter: off, then 16
steps from 4 to 64 times into y = 1.5x - 0.5x^3, turned back down so that the game's music gets
1 to 4 dB louder across the knob. Steps are ramped across a block and off/on is a crossfade.
i_oplmusic.c: with fm1_music_instr set, every melodic note is played on that one of GENMIDI's 128
instruments (percussion is left alone); the knob says the instrument's name on the message line.
EDIT now turns off the filter, the drive and the instrument together.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
